"label": "Results",
"text": "In all patients, at least one mutation in cfDNA was detected at diagnosis. CREBBP was the most frequent mutated gene (67 %). In 12 of the 15 patients with complete remission, the mutation attributed to the disease found at diagnosis cleared with treatment. A reduction in the ctDNA was observed after treatment in 14 patients, 12 of whom achieved complete remission. Correlations were found between the ctDNA at diagnosis and total metabolic tumor volume (r = 0.51; p-value = 0.014) and total lesion glycolysis 2.5 (r = 0.47; p-value = 0.024) by PET at diagnosis and between ctDNA at diagnosis and radiomic features of the lesions with the largest standardized uptake value. There was a strong inverse correlation between ΔctDNA1 and ΔSUVmax by PET/CT (r = -0.8788; p-value = 0.002)."
},
